Generate {{ num_docs }} English texts simulating partially redacted documents where some PII remains visible.

## Purpose
In production, partially anonymized documents are re-processed. This tests detection of residual PII alongside redaction markers.

## Rules
- Tag ONLY the remaining (visible) PII
- Do NOT tag redacted/hidden content

## Patterns

### Name partially redacted
- "Applicant: [REDACTED] (contact: <PERSON>Sarah Mitchell</PERSON>)"
- "Name: **** Supervisor: <PERSON>Dr. James Rivera</PERSON>"
- "Author: ████████ Editor: <PERSON>Maria Santos</PERSON>"

### Address partially redacted
- "Home: [REDACTED] Office: <ADDRESS>200 West Street, New York, NY 10282</ADDRESS>"
- "Previous: ████████ Current: <ADDRESS>456 Palm Avenue, Los Angeles, CA 90001</ADDRESS>"

### Mixed redacted and visible PII
"Claimant [REDACTED] (DOB: <DATE_OF_BIRTH>June 3, 1989</DATE_OF_BIRTH>) resides at [REDACTED ADDRESS].
Employer: <ORGANIZATION>Meridian Health Systems</ORGANIZATION>
Account: [REDACTED] → Updated to: <BANK_ACCOUNT>Wells Fargo, Routing: 121000248, Account: 776543210, Savings</BANK_ACCOUNT>"

### Template placeholders mixed with real data
- "{name} <PERSON>Kevin Park</PERSON> {address} <ADDRESS>1600 Amphitheatre Pkwy, Mountain View, CA 94043</ADDRESS>"
- "<<FIRST_NAME>> <PERSON>Rosa Gutierrez</PERSON> <<LAST_NAME>>"

### Redaction markers that look like PII
- "[Person Name Redacted]" (no tag - this is a redaction marker)
- "XXX-XX-1234" (partial SSN, no tag)
- "[Address Removed]" (no tag)

## Confusing expressions (NO tags)
- Redaction markers: "[REDACTED]", "████", "****", "[REMOVED]"
- Placeholders: "{name}", "<<FIELD>>", "[PLACEHOLDER]"
- "Example:" prefixed sample data
- Partial values: "***-**-1234", "J*** S****"

## Output format
Separate each text with `---DOC_SEPARATOR---`. Each text 80-300 words.
